  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Specifically, in the simple display of the world list that appears when performing a world search, a world with a capacity of 32 is displayed as having a capacity of 64.\n\nIf you go to the individual world page, the correct capacity will be displayed.\n\nSometimes this happens even for worlds with a capacity of 16 (in this case, 32 is displayed).\n\nOn the other hand, there are some worlds where this does not happen even for worlds with a capacity of 32, so I am not sure of the law of this phenomenon.\n\nIn other worlds, such as those with 20, 24, or 30 people, this phenomenon does not seem to occur.\n\nPlease take measures to ensure that the capacity is displayed correctly.\n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
